---
source: tests/relogin.rs
expression: "shown(&d, &m.f)"
---

--relogin: not logging out. 1 of 6 check(s) did not pass:
  ok  switch   generation 0001 is current
  NO  journal  <HOME>/.local/state/ricepilot/journal/current.toml exists: an operation is in flight and did not finish.
               `ricepilot recover` first; a machine half way through something is not one to log in to
  ok  rescue   <HOME>/.local/state/ricepilot/rescue.sh restores generation 0000 and passes `sh -n`
  ok  links    3 link(s) are exactly what the plan said and what the ledger recorded
  ok  lock     this ricepilot holds <HOME>/.run/ricepilot.lock, and it is still the file at that path
  ok  session  WAYLAND_DISPLAY=wayland-1 is there in XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, uwsm's wayland-wm@hyprland.desktop.service is running,
               nothing says ssh, tmux or screen, and the controlling terminal was not looked at (test sandbox)

nothing was run. the switch itself is complete: generation 0001 is what the next login
starts. ricepilot ends a session only when every check above passes.
